conventions = [
    'Layer spacing is d(hkl) divided by the number of layers per repeat, also when the layers are unevenly spaced; the page note "middle plane to middle plane" holds only for even spacing (A3-05, A5-02).',
    'Organic gallery is that mean spacing minus the slab of the first layer of the cell; it is a face-to-face distance only for identical, evenly spaced layers (A3-05, A5-02).',
    'Slab, gallery and stacking offset are computed for the first layer of the cell and its upper neighbour only; with two unlike interfaces the picture can show the other one (A5-03, A3-10).',
    'Stacking offset: which metal of each layer is used, and that the two numbers are folded along the two shortest non-parallel M...M vectors (not the nearest metal over all pairs) (A3-01).',
    'Metal heights closer than 1.5 A count as one metal plane, and n is reported also for face- and edge-sharing layers (A3-07).',
    'A face plane takes the terminal halides (bonded to one metal) more than 1.0 A beyond the outermost metal plane (A3-10).',
    'Axial bonds are those within 45.6 deg of the layer normal (|cos| > 0.7); equatorial bridges have M...M within 60 deg of the layer plane (A3-10).',
    'Ammonium N: exactly four neighbours with at least two H (an N with H in two orientations has more and is skipped), or one heavy neighbour when the file has no H at all; only N within 3 A of a face get a penetration (A3-10, DA-b02).',
    'Offset labels use a tolerance of 0.15 (A3-10).',
    'Hydrogen bonds: an N with four bonds is never an acceptor; files without H use N/O...halide contacts below the vdW sum + 0.15 A (README lacks this; page text has it) (A3-10).',
    'Halide-halide, H-H and H-halide pairs are never covalently bonded (DA-b05).',
    'Mn, Fe and Co use the low-spin Cordero radii (A3-10).',
    'Slab, gallery and penetration assume flat (100)-type layers; corrugated (110) layers give interpenetrating face planes (DA-b04).',
    'The metal-halide cut-off is sharp: a bridge 0.02 A above it splits a slab and changes n and the spacing (DA-b01).',
    'Framework metals are drawn only when inside the packing block, so the default block can cut a layer in half (A5-01).',
    'Torsions are shown to 0.1 deg, other angles to 0.01 deg (A5-09).',
    'The "1x" PNG has the canvas pixels of 3Dmol, twice the CSS size at device pixel ratio 1 (A5-12).',
    'At most 20 measurements are kept; the oldest is dropped (A6-09).',
    'Symbol-only CIFs of two-origin groups get origin choice 1 (A6-05 = A2-05).',
    'For a cell of more than 400 atoms the hydrogen bonds are searched in one cell only (A3-03; this is a bug to fix, not only a convention to state).',
    'Means in the Structures table are unweighted means over independent sites (or distinct bridges), as the column tooltip says; for files without symmetry every atom is a site (DA-b06).',
]

